From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:24:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libnativeloader: answer the namespace lookups when there are
 no namespaces

Without ART_TARGET_ANDROID libnativeloader exports no FindNamespaceByClassLoader / FindNativeLoaderNamespaceByClassLoader, which its lazy wrapper (native_loader_lazy.cpp) and libandroid_runtime's GraphicsEnvironment.setLayerPaths call; the wrapper dlsym()s them and, with LOG_FATAL_IF compiled out, calls the null result, so every app start crashed at GraphicsEnvironment.setLayerPaths. Both now return nullptr: no class loader has a namespace.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: the symbols are libnativeloader's own API, looked up in libnativeloader.so by name; no launcher flag, loader setting or library elsewhere can define them there, and the ART_TARGET_LINUX configuration (chosen so ART needs no bionic linker) leaves out the only definitions
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 libnativeloader/native_loader.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libnativeloader/native_loader.cpp b/libnativeloader/native_loader.cpp
index 964279446fa315e29d180089cb2b8ed36560073e..1a4e6a6d3d1f29186b386cdf71c736e57cc97e38 100644
--- a/libnativeloader/native_loader.cpp
+++ b/libnativeloader/native_loader.cpp
@@ -587,6 +587,13 @@ void LinkNativeLoaderNamespaceToExportedNamespaceLibrary(struct NativeLoaderName
   }
 }
 
+#else  // !ART_TARGET_ANDROID
+
+// No linker namespaces without bionic's linker: no class loader has one.
+android_namespace_t* FindNamespaceByClassLoader(JNIEnv*, jobject) { return nullptr; }
+
+NativeLoaderNamespace* FindNativeLoaderNamespaceByClassLoader(JNIEnv*, jobject) { return nullptr; }
+
 #endif  // ART_TARGET_ANDROID
 
 }  // namespace android
